#
# Shell completion for `kubectl patchy …`.
#
# kubectl (1.26+) does not read the plugin's own completion script. When the
# user tabs after a plugin name it strips its own global flags, looks for an
# executable called kubectl_complete-<plugin> on PATH, and runs it with the
# remaining words — so this file has to be installed alongside kubectl-patchy,
# not into a shell's completion directory. Whatever it prints is consumed
# verbatim: cobra's __complete protocol, one candidate per line followed by a
# `:<directive>` line.
#
# kubectl-patchy already speaks that protocol, so forwarding is the whole job.

kubectl-patchy __complete "$@"
